WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.350
- [Narrator] Earth, the only
planet known to maintain life.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.783
A product of scientific
phenomena and sheer chance.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.520
This blue speck in space holds the past,

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.048
present, and future,
of our very existence.

00:00:17.048 --> 00:00:19.900
(instrumental music)

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.750
Approximately 4.5 billion years ago,

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.601
the Earth formed from particles left over

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.210
from the creation of our sun.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.090
Gravity drew these particles together

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:31.860
to form pebbles which
then formed boulders,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.663
and eventually, the Earth.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.040
At its heart is a solid inner core

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.400
covered by a liquid outer core.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.459
Above this sits the mantle,
made of flowing silicate rocks,

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:44.653
and a rocky crust.

00:00:45.681 --> 00:00:49.210
This rocky mass is the
third planet from the sun,

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.510
orbiting the star from an average distance

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.963
of about 93 million miles.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.090
It's close enough to the sun to be warm

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.350
unlike the cold gas giants.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.240
But not so close that its surface

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.460
is exposed to extreme
heat and solar radiation

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.173
as is the case with Mercury.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.824
Earth's unique position
in the solar system

00:01:09.824 --> 00:01:11.860
allows it to house phenomena

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.800
yet to be found anywhere
else in the universe,

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.013
particularly liquid
surface water and life.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.250
According to one theory,
much of Earth's water

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.154
is as old as its rocks,
both of which having formed

00:01:25.154 --> 00:01:27.423
during the Earth's earliest days.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.310
Because of Earth's unique
distance from the sun,

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.270
the planet is able to contain water

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.494
in all of its forms, liquid, ice and gas

00:01:36.494 --> 00:01:39.040
rather than have them permanently frozen

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.143
or evaporated into space.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.700
But Earth is the only
known place in the universe

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.930
with liquid water on the surface,

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.670
thereby having unique cascading
effects on the planet.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.720
It hydrates the land helping
create nutrient rich soil.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.160
It collects and pools to form
oceans and freshwater systems.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:03.660
And it cycles upward to add moisture

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.643
to Earth's protective atmosphere.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.620
And where there is liquid
water, there is life.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.240
About 3.8 billion years
ago in Earth's oceans

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.315
primitive life existed in the
form of microbial organisms.

00:02:21.315 --> 00:02:23.974
They and the ensuing billions of years

00:02:23.974 --> 00:02:27.440
gave rise to a range of
more advanced life forms

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.913
that survived in Earth's
seas, lands and skies.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.430
As the only world known to harbor life,

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.553
Earth's biodiversity
is expansive in nature.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:45.542
An estimated 1.5 million
species of plants,

00:02:45.542 --> 00:02:49.300
animals, bacteria, fungi and others

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.892
have been cataloged with
potentially millions,

00:02:51.892 --> 00:02:56.003
if not billions more yet to be discovered.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.111
Home to life and fueled by water,

00:03:00.111 --> 00:03:03.810
Earth houses a unique global ecosystem

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.729
as curious and as grand
as the astronomical events

00:03:06.729 --> 00:03:08.633
that made them possible.

